5. FY2027 BUDGET WORKSHOP (fiscal year January 1 - December 31, 2027)
   Ms. Marsh presented the draft FY27 operating ($9.84M) and capital ($3.12M)
   budgets. Wholesale rate to member towns held flat at $2.41 / 1,000 gal.

   Capital items discussed:
     a. Summit Tank mixing system ...................... $  410,000  (keep)
     b. Hilltop PS-3 VFD replacement (P-301) ........... $  265,000  (keep)
     c. Miller Creek crossing (1962 cast iron) - replace
        with HDD crossing ............................... $1,900,000  (FY29)
        Mr. Pruitt reminded the Board that until the crossing is replaced,
        the surge protection at Hilltop PS-3 is the only thing keeping a
        pump trip or fast valve closure from overstressing that segment.
     d. OT security improvements (deferred from FY26) .. $  186,000
        Ms. Whitfield reported the state cybersecurity grant application was
        not funded in the first round. Directors asked staff to bring back a
        reduced scope. Item remains DEFERRED; to be revisited at the
        FY27 Q1 meeting. Staff to proceed with no-cost items in the meantime
        "as time allows."

   No action taken; final budget adoption scheduled for November 19, 2026.

